{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UmJzufHcZqBusWgSTW9jyx","type":"tool_result","content":"151:## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n152-\n153-- Status baseline: pending\n154-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n155-- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n156-- Objective: Create/maintain the `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS` root and per-order folder trees; upload with naming convention; write-once original-request folder.\n157-- Context: `architecture.md §5`, master doc §12.\n158-- Scope: `drive.ensureRoot()`, `drive.createOrderFolders(ticketId, customerName)` (subfolders 00–07), `drive.storeFile(ticketId, category, blob)` applying naming `ORD-…_*`, Documents row per file, `immutable=true` for category original_request; customer folders under `01_CUSTOMERS`.\n159-- Out of scope: UI upload widgets (APP-002).\n160-- Architectural invariants: nothing in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` is ever overwritten/deleted; every stored file gets a Documents row.\n161-- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/drive/**`\n162-- Deliverables: module + test evidence.\n163-- Verification (per ADR-005 — split local/live, no live-only acceptance path):\n164-  - **Local:** static review of folder-tree/naming logic against `architecture.md §5`; immutability guard on `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` reviewed in code (rejection path present, not bypassable).\n165-  - **Live:** requires real Google Drive access (same account/OAuth as INF-002). Command: run test creating order tree, storing file in each category, attempting overwrite in original_request (expect rejection), verifying Documents rows. If unavailable, report `blocked-external-verification` naming missing Drive/OAuth access.\n166-- Acceptance criteria: local tier — tree/naming/immutability logic matches spec. Live tier — tree matches spec exactly; overwrite rejected; rows correct. May accept `completed-local / pending-live-verification` if only live tier blocked by credentials.\n167-- Rollback notes: test folders under a `_TEST` prefix, deletable.\n168-- Architect notes: use Drive folder IDs in Documents, not paths.\n169-\n170-## APP-001 — Customers Module\n171-\n172-- Status baseline: pending\n173-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n174-- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n175-- Objective: Customer CRUD (soft delete) + search, per `data-model.md#Customers`, roles M/S.\n176-- Context: `permissions-matrix.md`.\n177-- Scope: API actions create/update/list/search/deactivate; duplicate warning on (`id_type`,`id_number`); UI form + list (Spanish).\n178-- Out of scope: purchase history, credit fields.\n179-- Architectural invariants: billing role read-only here; required fields enforced server-side.\n180-- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/customers/**`, `src/ui/customers/**`\n181-- Deliverables: module + UI.\n182-- Verification commands: API tests: create valid/invalid, duplicate detection, billing-role write rejected.\n183-- Acceptance criteria: tests PASS; UI usable end-to-end.\n184-- Rollback notes: module-scoped; remove files.\n185-- Architect notes: —\n186-\n187-## APP-002 — Tickets Module + Intake\n188-\n189-- Status baseline: pending\n190-- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n191-- Dependencies: [APP-001, INF-003]\n192-- Objective: Ticket creation (ID `ORD-YYYYMM-NNNN`), intake channel capture, advisor assignment, Drive case file auto-created, original request upload (immutable), ticket read/update per schema.\n193-- Context: `data-model.md#Tickets`; stage 1 of the journey.\n194-- Scope: create ticket (state `received`, `last_activity_at`, Activity row); upload original request via INF-003; edit non-workflow fields (notes, priority, labels, next_action, waiting_on); list with filters.\n195-- Out of scope: state transitions (APP-003), parts, quotations.\n196-- Architectural invariants: ticket always has customer, channel, advisor; original request immutable; monthly sequence atomic.\n197-- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/tickets/**`, `src/ui/tickets/**`\n198-- Deliverables: module + intake UI.\n199-- Verification commands: tests: ID format/sequence across month boundary; folder created; original upload locked; Activity rows.\n200-- Acceptance criteria: create→view→edit cycle works; invariants verified.\n201-- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n202-- Architect notes: month boundary sequence test is mandatory.\n203-\n204-## APP-003 — Workflow State Machine Engine\n205-\n206-- Status baseline: pending\n207-- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n208-- Dependencies: [APP-002]\n209-- Objective: Server-enforced transitions per `workflow-state-machine.md`: matrix from Configuration, role checks, guards, Activity logging, clear invalid-transition errors listing allowed targets.\n210-- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` is normative including all 8 guards.\n211-- Scope: `workflow.transition(ticketId, toState, meta)`; guard framework (evidence checks, role checks, quotation/payment prerequisites as pluggable predicates — predicates for not-yet-built modules return \"guard dependency missing\" and block); `lost` from any non-terminal with mandatory reason; M reopen exception.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50e8cbd0-7cab-4a32-a911-487d2caf7b4b","uuid":"9ae0d83e-51a7-4332-b165-61f628146782","timestamp":"2026-07-22T02:19:01.560Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"151:## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n152-\n153-- Status baseline: pending\n154-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n155-- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n156-- Objective: Create/maintain the `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS` root and per-order folder trees; upload with naming convention; write-once original-request folder.\n157-- Context: `architecture.md §5`, master doc §12.\n158-- Scope: `drive.ensureRoot()`, `drive.createOrderFolders(ticketId, customerName)` (subfolders 00–07), `drive.storeFile(ticketId, category, blob)` applying naming `ORD-…_*`, Documents row per file, `immutable=true` for category original_request; customer folders under `01_CUSTOMERS`.\n159-- Out of scope: UI up